articles=[
 dict(slug='before-you-file', category='Litigation', title='Before a suit is filed: five questions worth answering', summary='The right claim in the wrong forum can lose time before the merits are reached.', read='4 min read', paragraphs=[
 ('Start with the remedy','A grievance and a legal remedy are not always the same thing. Before drafting, define the order you actually need: a declaration, an injunction, payment, possession or another form of relief. That choice affects jurisdiction, evidence and the pleadings.'),
 ('Identify the right forum','Questions of territorial, subject-matter and pecuniary jurisdiction should be addressed at the beginning. A specialist statute may direct a dispute away from an ordinary civil suit. Applicable law and current limits must be checked for the particular matter.'),
 ('Build a chronology','Dates, notices, payments and communications often determine the shape of the case. Put the documents in order and distinguish what is known from what remains to be proved.'),
 ('Check time and interim risk','Limitation periods, procedural deadlines and the need for urgent interim protection may change the order in which work must be done. A delay can matter even when the underlying claim has substance.'),
 ('Price the dispute realistically','Litigation has financial and commercial costs. Compare the likely course of proceedings with settlement, negotiation and other legally available avenues. The best route is one chosen with its risks understood.')]),
 dict(slug='banking-record', category='Banking & finance', title='In a banking dispute, the record matters', summary='A useful first review looks beyond the outstanding figure to the facility, security and correspondence.', read='3 min read', paragraphs=[
 ('Begin with the transaction','The central document may be a facility agreement, but it is rarely the only relevant one. Guarantees, security instruments, renewals, account statements and subsequent communications can all affect the questions in dispute.'),
 ('Separate the obligations','A borrower, guarantor and security provider may have distinct legal positions. The answer depends on the actual documents and the relevant law, not a general assumption that everyone carries identical liability.'),
 ('Keep the chronology intact','Drawdowns, repayments, notices and changes to facilities should be placed in sequence. A reliable chronology assists both legal analysis and the practical discussion of a dispute.'),
 ('Review the available route','Forum, remedy and procedure turn on the relationship, nature of the finance and applicable statutory framework. These should be identified before litigation strategy is settled.')]),
 dict(slug='commercial-contracts', category='Corporate & commercial', title='The clauses that deserve more attention', summary='Clear contracts assign risk before the parties need to argue about it.', read='3 min read', paragraphs=[
 ('Scope and performance','A contract should describe what each party must deliver and how performance will be measured. Vague obligations can become expensive factual disputes.'),
 ('Payment and default','The timing of invoices, payment, interest or other contractual consequences, termination and cure periods should be aligned rather than scattered across contradictory provisions.'),
 ('Change and exit','Commercial relationships evolve. A sound agreement anticipates changes in scope, assignment, termination, notices and what remains payable when the relationship ends.'),
 ('Dispute clauses','Governing law, jurisdiction, arbitration arrangements and notice provisions should be understood before signing. A standard clause copied without attention to the transaction can create avoidable uncertainty.')]),
]

